                <pb facs="0455" n="343" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg343"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 24074/8.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Calhoun to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-04-30"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">April 30,
                    1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Calhoun refers to his April 22, and says that Military Attaché Reeves, who is
                    on a tour of inspection has arrived at Hankow, and that the legation has
                    requested him to go to Chang-sha, especially with a view to ascertaining the
                    extent of the damage done to American property.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
